 "sections": [
  {
   "type": "paragraph",
   "text": "All Disciplines"
  },
  {
   "type": "paragraph",
   "text": "Instruction:\n Coding \n System \n for MPIS Documents"
  },
  {
   "type": "paragraph",
   "text": "The address \n of the MPIS document is identified at the header of the first page, which \n indicates the discipline type \"All disciplines\" and the document type \n \"Administration Instructions\" the first revision \n 06 Feb 2002, revised at 01 Jan 2003, and 11 March \n 2003."
  },
  {
   "type": "paragraph",
   "text": "In order to manage the documents produced in MPIS it is necessary to give \n each one a unique identifying number. Following are the standard \n abbreviations, which have been adopted and will be used as a code numbers for \n MPIS documents."
  },
  {
   "type": "paragraph",
   "text": "Also the document number is created to facilitate various sorting and \n retrieval processes i.e. to help people how to store any MPIS document or \n retrieve it from its right location in the binder."
  },
  {
