  {
   "type": "paragraph",
   "text": "Each document will be reviewed on a predetermined frequency. There may be \n revisions required as a result of these reviews. There are also occasions when \n the requirement for revisions are discovered when a document is applied in a \n new location. There must be a code to identify the number of revisions which \n have been made to a document, for example r0 = original approved document, r1 \n = first revision after approval etc."
  },
  {
   "type": "paragraph",
   "text": "As mentioned in the introduction the coding system applied to MPIS documents \n is intended to provide important information about the document to facilitate \n various sorting and retrieval processes."
  },
  {
   "type": "paragraph",
   "text": "The first 2 or 3 letters will indicate the equipment type, the second set \n of numbers will indicate the sequence number, the final 2 numbers indicate the \n number of times the document has been reviewed/revised, and we will add small \n letter ( a ) to indicate the language of the document is Arabic."
  },
  {
   "type": "paragraph",
   "text": "Following is an example of a typical MPIS \n Technical Procedures, document code number derived from \n this method:"
  },
  {
   "type": "paragraph",
   "text": "Equipment Type"
  },
  {
   "type": "paragraph",
   "text": "Sequence Number"
  },
  {
   "type": "paragraph",
   "text": "Review / Revision Number"
  },
  {
   "type": "paragraph",
   "text": "Arabic"
  },
  {
   "type": "paragraph",
   "text": "CB"
  },
  {
   "type": "paragraph",
   "text": "001"
  },
  {
   "type": "paragraph",
   "text": "r0"
  },
  {
   "type": "paragraph",
   "text": "a"
  },
  {
   "type": "paragraph",
   "text": "Explanation of Above Example:\nCB-001-r0a\n CB = Circuit Breaker 001 = Document sequence number \nr0 = No. of Review/Revision, r1 = Revision no.1 after the\n first approval process. \na \n = Arabic document.\n Also the following is an another example of a typical MPIS Technical Directives \nor Bulletins document code number derived from this method:"
  },
  {
   "type": "paragraph",
   "text": "Document type"
  },
  {
   "type": "paragraph",
   "text": "Sequence Number"
  },
  {
   "type": "paragraph",
   "text": "Review / Revision Number"
  },
  {
   "type": "paragraph",
   "text": "Arabic"
  },
  {
   "type": "paragraph",
   "text": "TB"
  },
  {
   "type": "paragraph",
   "text": "001"
  },
  {
   "type": "paragraph",
   "text": "r0"
  },
  {
   "type": "paragraph",
   "text": "a"
  },
  {
   "type": "paragraph",
   "text": "Explanation of the above Example: \n TB-SS-001-r0a"
  },
  {
   "type": "paragraph",
   "text": "TB = Technical Bulletin, \nSS = Substations, \n001 = Document sequence \n no.r0 = No. of Review/Revision, r1: means Revision no.1 after the \nfirst approval processa \n = Arabic document."
  }
 ],
 "text": "All Disciplines\nInstruction:\n Coding \n System \n for MPIS Documents\nThe address \n of the MPIS document is identified at the header of the first page, which \n indicates the discipline type \"All disciplines\" and the document type \n \"Administration Instructions\" the first revision \n 06 Feb 2002, revised at 01 Jan 2003, and 11 March \n 2003.\nIn order to manage the documents produced in MPIS it is necessary to give \n each one a unique identifying number. Following are the standard \n abbreviations, which have been adopted and will be used as a code numbers for \n MPIS documents.\nAlso the document number is created to facilitate various sorting and \n retrieval processes i.e. to help people how to store any MPIS document or \n retrieve it from its right location in the binder.\nThe Egyptian Electricity Holding Company consist of 14 Companies for\n generation, transmission, and distribution\nProposed Codes for Companies\nEgyptian Company for Electricity Transmission 1 Company\nCode\nIdentification\nCode\nIdentification\n1\nCairo Zone\n5\nMiddle \n Egypt\n2\nAlexandria and West Delta Zone\n6\nUpper \n Egypt\n3\nCanal Zone\n7\n4\nDelta \n Zone\nElectricity Distribution\nCompanies 9 Companies\nCode\nIdentification\nCode\nIdentification\n1\n6\nNorth Delta\n2\n3\nAlexandria\n8\nMiddle Egypt\n4\nEl_Behaira\nUpper Egypt\n5\nCanal\nElectricity \nProduction Companies \n 6 Companies\nCode\nIdentification\nCode\nIdentification\n1\nProposed Codes for Transmission Voltage Levels\nCode Letter\nKV\nColor Code\nCode Letter\nKV\nColor Code\nCode Letter\nKV\nColor Code\nA\n500\nRed\nD\n66\nBlue\nG\n11\nWhite\nB\n220\nGreen\nE\n33\nBlack\nC\n132\nYellow\nF\n20\nMagenta\nProposed Codes for Work Groups \n(Disciplines)\nCode\nIdentification\nCode\nIdentification\nSS\nSubstations\nPC\nProtection and Control\nCom\nCommunication\nTL\nTransmission Line\nCab\nCables\nG\nGeneration\n\nProposed Codes for Document Types\nCode\nIdentification\nCode\nIdentification\nTP\nTechnical Procedures\nTD\nTechnical Directive\nTB\nTechnical Bulletin\nMRDS\nMaintenance Record Data Sheet\nCL\nCheck List\nAI\nAdministrative Instructions\nProposed Codes for Substations Equipment\nCode\nIdentification\nCode\nIdentification\nCS\nCoding System\nSD\nSystem Drawings\nAS\nAir Supply System\nB\nBattery\nBB\nBus Bar\nBkP\nBack Portion \"GIS Compartments\"\nCB\nCircuit Breaker\nCap\nCapacitor\nCh\nCharger\nCP\nCompressor Plant\nCT\nCurrent Transformer\nDS\nDisconnect Switch\nDsl\nDiesel\nES\nEarthing Switch\nET\nEarthing Transformer\nFS\nFire Fighting System\nGIS\nGas Insulated System\nLA\nLightning (Surge) Arrestor\nPT\nPotential Transformer\nSF6\nSulfur Hexa-floride Gas\nT\nTransformer\nTC\nTap Changer\nTU\nTest unit\nUPS\nUn-interrupter Power Supply or Inverter\nX\nReactor\nCam\nCamera\n\nProposed Codes for Protection Relays Types\nCode\nIdentification\nCode\nIdentification\nDsR\nDistance Protection Relay\nBBP\nBus Bar Protection\nEFR\nEarth Fault Relay\nOCR\nOver Current Relay\nDfR\nDifferential Protection Relay\nOVR\nOver Voltage Relay\nUVR\nUnder Voltage \n Relay\nMD\nMetering Device\nFR\nFault Recorder\nER\nEvent Recorder\n\nProposed Codes for Communication Instrument Types\nCode\nIdentification\nCode\nIdentification\nMw\nMicrowave\nFO\nFiber \n Optic\nPLC\nPower Line Carrier\nPABX\nExchange \n Switch\nRTU\nRemote Terminal Unit\nTelP\nTele \n Protection\nProposed Codes for Transmission Lines Component\nCode\nIdentification\nCode\nIdentification\nST\nStructure Of Tower\nIns\nInsulators\nW\nWire Of Conductor\nSp\nSpacer\nR\nRope\nH\nHook\nSH\nSafety and Health\nProposed Codes for Chemical Component\nCode\nIdentification\nCode\nIdentification\nEnv\nPol\nPollution\nCode\nIdentification\nCode\nIdentification\nG\nGenerator\nBlr\nBoiler\nExc\nExciter\nTR\nTrash \n Rackes\nP\nPump\nGT\n\nEach document will be reviewed on a predetermined frequency. There may be \n revisions required as a result of these reviews. There are also occasions when \n the requirement for revisions are discovered when a document is applied in a \n new location. There must be a code to identify the number of revisions which \n have been made to a document, for example r0 = original approved document, r1 \n = first revision after approval etc.\nAs mentioned in the introduction the coding system applied to MPIS documents \n is intended to provide important information about the document to facilitate \n various sorting and retrieval processes.\nThe first 2 or 3 letters will indicate the equipment type, the second set \n of numbers will indicate the sequence number, the final 2 numbers indicate the \n number of times the document has been reviewed/revised, and we will add small \n letter ( a ) to indicate the language of the document is Arabic.\nFollowing is an example of a typical MPIS \n Technical Procedures, document code number derived from \n this method:\nEquipment Type\nSequence Number\nReview / Revision Number\nArabic\nCB\n001\nr0\na\nExplanation of Above Example:\nCB-001-r0a\n CB = Circuit Breaker 001 = Document sequence number \nr0 = No. of Review/Revision, r1 = Revision no.1 after the\n first approval process. \na \n = Arabic document.\n Also the following is an another example of a typical MPIS Technical Directives \nor Bulletins document code number derived from this method:\nDocument type\nSequence Number\nReview / Revision Number\nArabic\nTB\n001\nr0\na\nExplanation of the above Example: \n TB-SS-001-r0a\nTB = Technical Bulletin, \nSS = Substations, \n001 = Document sequence \n no.r0 = No. of Review/Revision, r1: means Revision no.1 after the \nfirst approval processa \n = Arabic document.",
